{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:18cacf0fab245b29","name":"Outbound Flight","source":{"id":"source:reference-18cacf0fab245b29","title":"Outbound Flight","revision":18768,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T20:42:11Z","sha256":"93f426c665dc99145335228f590b714ed7c619166b3cd5dafbfad635bb907364","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=18768","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Outbound%20Flight&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-18cacf0fab245b29","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi","referenceId":"reference:d320edb17de6c558"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Republic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Republic","referenceId":"reference:332055cafc4223eb"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Outbound Flight Project was a mission whose goal was to explore the farthest reaches of the galaxy and beyond. An exploratory mission originally proposed by ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi","referenceId":"reference:d320edb17de6c558"},", the Outbound Flight Project became the personnel project of Jedi Master ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jorus C'baoth"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jorus_C%27baoth?action=edit&redlink=1"},", who fought with the Senate at every turn to get the project funded and underway. The Outbound Flight Project was created not only to explore new places, but also to set up colonies and- unbeknownst to all but a few of C'baoth's confidants- find new Force-sensitive apprentices to bolster the numbers of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi Order"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi_Order"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["However, the grand exploratory mission did not go as planned. In the Republic's first encounter with the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Chiss"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Chiss","referenceId":"reference:bd57eaad77f8edcc"}," that would eventually go on to become ",{"tag":"a","children":["Grand Admiral Thrawn"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Grand_Admiral_Thrawn"},", the Outbound Flight Project was derailed and the ship was lost, never reaching its destination in ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Unknown Regions"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Unknown_Regions"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Capabilities"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["The Outbound Flight Project revolved around the use of a massive ship, appropriately called ",{"tag":"i","children":["Outbound Flight"]},", that was comprised of six ",{"tag":"a","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Dreadnaught"]},"-Class Heavy Cruisers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dreadnaught-Class_Heavy_Cruiser","referenceId":"reference:0d13a1c3c7f04e82"}," arranged in a ring around a central fuselage, all connected by a web of metal that made all the vessels into a single, massive ship. The central fuselage carried the supplies needed to feed the crewmembers and passengers aboard ",{"tag":"i","children":["Outbound Flight"]}," for the duration of its journey, and also carried the relevant material for colonizing any habitable planets the explorers discovered.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Each of the ",{"tag":"a","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Dreadnaught"]},"-Class Heavy Cruisers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dreadnaught-Class_Heavy_Cruisers"}," was connected to the central fuselage and to each other by a series of access tunnels, and crewmembers could move between the six ",{"tag":"i","children":["Dreadnaughts"]}," or the central core by means of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Speeders"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Speeders","referenceId":"reference:be93ac2e4867f0ca"}," kept aboard for just that reason. Additionally, each ",{"tag":"a","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Dreadnaught"]},"-Class Heavy Cruiser"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dreadnaught-Class_Heavy_Cruiser","referenceId":"reference:0d13a1c3c7f04e82"}," could be detached from the central core, and it would do so in order to remain behind and protect any colonies the mission might find.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Skilled)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Outbound Flight"]}," Statistics (CL 22)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Colossal (Station) ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ship"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," -6; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +6\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 11 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 11), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 114; +13 Armor, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicular Combat"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicular_Combat","referenceId":"reference:31246426131b3457"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","referenceId":"reference:58e8ee2c9538d027"},": 9,000; ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Reduction"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Reduction"},": 20; ",{"tag":"a","children":["Shield Rating"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Shield_Rating"},": 165; ",{"